---
id: org.dxos.echo-sync-worker
name: EchoSyncWorker
version: 0.1.0
---

`@dxos/echo-sync-worker` is the server half of echo-sqlite sync: a Cloudflare Worker that routes
each graph to one Durable Object, `SpaceObject`, which holds the authoritative copy of that graph's
records and orders every write to it. The client half is `org.dxos.echo-sqlite-sync`.

Three properties define it:

- **Order comes from counters, never from clocks.** The object stamps each accepted write with the
  graph's next `seq`, and each client numbers its own pushes with `clientSeq` [F-1]. No wall-clock
  time decides which write wins.
- **A write is applied only on top of what its writer saw.** Every pushed record names the `seq` it
  was edited on; the object applies a push only if all of them are still current, and otherwise
  answers with what the client missed [F-2].
- **The directory deploys alone.** It imports nothing outside itself and pins its tools by version,
  so the "Deploy to Cloudflare" button can copy it into a new repository and build it with npm [F-6].

Tests: the object's behaviour runs in workerd in `@dxos/echo-sqlite-sync`'s
`space-object.workerd.test.ts` (T-1 to T-6).

## Dependencies

None. This spec is the base of the sync pair.

