## Diagrams

Diagrams are plugin-illustrator renders. The `diagram` block is the source; regenerate the image with
`moon run plugin-illustrator:render-diagrams -- <abs path>/diagrams/<name>.dx`.

### A push, accepted

![Client A pushes records based on seq 4 since seq 4; the object checks each base against its entries, stamps seq 5 and 6, records clientSeq 3 for A, answers A with an ack carrying the records with their seqs, and sends the same records to client B as a records message from 4 to 6.](diagrams/push-accepted.dx.svg)

```diagram
diagram kind=sequence
node A "client A" ref="packages/core/echo/echo-sqlite-sync/src/sync.ts"
node DO "SpaceObject" ref="packages/core/echo/echo-sync-worker/src/space-object.ts"
node Store "entries" ref="packages/core/echo/echo-sync-worker/src/space-object.ts"
node B "client B" ref="packages/core/echo/echo-sqlite-sync/src/sync.ts"
edge A sends DO "push since=4"
edge DO calls Store "seq of each key"
edge Store returns DO "all equal base"
edge DO calls Store "write seq 5, 6"
edge Store returns DO "applied"
note DO "client:A = 3"
edge DO sends A "ack accepted"
edge DO sends B "records 4..6"
```

### A push, rejected

![Client A pushes record x based on seq 2, but client B already moved x to seq 5; the object applies nothing and answers A with a rejected ack listing x as a conflict and carrying x at seq 5; A merges three-way and pushes again based on seq 5, which is accepted at seq 6 and broadcast to B.](diagrams/push-rejected.dx.svg)

```diagram
diagram kind=sequence
node A "client A" ref="packages/core/echo/echo-sqlite-sync/src/sync.ts"
node DO "SpaceObject" ref="packages/core/echo/echo-sync-worker/src/space-object.ts"
node B "client B" ref="packages/core/echo/echo-sqlite-sync/src/sync.ts"
edge B sends DO "push x base=2"
edge DO sends B "ack accepted, x@5"
edge DO sends A "records x@5"
edge A sends DO "push x base=2"
edge DO sends A "ack rejected [x]"
note A "merge3(x@2, mine, x@5)"
edge A sends DO "push x base=5"
edge DO sends A "ack accepted, x@6"
edge DO sends B "records x@6"
```

The second push from A is the race this guards: A sent it before the broadcast of x@5 reached it.

### Storage

![SpaceObject owns the entries table and the spaceState keyspace; the SPACE binding addresses one SpaceObject per slug; the sync and socket routes reach it through the binding.](diagrams/storage.dx.svg)

```diagram
diagram flow=down
node Sync "route sync" ref="packages/core/echo/echo-sync-worker/src/index.ts"
node Socket "route socket" ref="packages/core/echo/echo-sync-worker/src/index.ts"
node Space "binding SPACE" ref="packages/core/echo/echo-sync-worker/wrangler.jsonc"
node Object "SpaceObject" ref="packages/core/echo/echo-sync-worker/src/space-object.ts"
node Entries "table entries" ref="packages/core/echo/echo-sync-worker/src/space-object.ts"
node State "keyspace spaceState" ref="packages/core/echo/echo-sync-worker/src/space-object.ts"
edge Sync -> Space
edge Socket -> Space
edge Space -> Object "idFromName(slug)"
edge Object owns Entries
edge Object owns State
```

## Types

```mdl
type SyncRecord
  desc: |
    One object of a graph as it travels and as the store holds it. Identified by `key`, a foreign key
    the client keeps in `Obj.Meta.keys`, because the ECHO id is minted per instance and cannot be shared.
  fields:
    key: string                                       # stable across instances
    typename: string                                  # fully-qualified type DXN
    props: Record<string, unknown>                    # scalar properties
    refs: Record<string, string | string[] | null>    # edges by property, to other records' keys; null = cleared
    deleted?: boolean                                 # a tombstone
    seq?: number                                      # the store's stamp; absent on a record a client sends
```

```mdl
type PushRecord
  desc: A record as a client pushes it, naming the version it was edited on [F-2].
  extends: [SyncRecord]
  fields:
    base?: number    # the seq it was edited on; 0 = new; omitted = unconditional write
```

```mdl
type PushRequest
  desc: A push, as the socket's `push` message or the `sync` route's body.
  fields:
    client?: string             # names the client across reconnects
    clientSeq?: number          # the client's own counter, one per push
    since: number               # the highest seq the client has applied
    records: PushRecord[]
```

```mdl
type ClientMessage
  desc: What a client sends over the socket.
  literals: pull | push
  fields:
    pull: { since: number }
    push: PushRequest
```

```mdl
type StoreInfo
  desc: What every answer says about the store itself.
  fields:
    seq: number             # the store's highest seq
    incarnation: string     # minted with the store, dropped with it [F-5]
    expiresAt: number       # epoch ms
```

```mdl
type RecordsMessage
  desc: |
    Records in seq order covering everything above `from` up to `seq`: the answer to a `pull`, and
    the broadcast of another client's push. A client that has applied up to `from` may advance to `seq`.
  extends: [StoreInfo]
  fields:
    from: number
    records: SyncRecord[]
```

```mdl
type PushResult
  desc: |
    The answer to a push, to the pusher only. `records` is everything above the push's `since`: the
    pushed records with their new seqs when accepted, what the client missed when rejected.
  extends: [StoreInfo]
  fields:
    clientSeq?: number
    accepted: boolean
    conflicts: string[]     # keys whose base was not their current seq
    from: number
    records: SyncRecord[]
```

## Worker

```mdl
binding SPACE: The namespace of graph objects; the router addresses one per slug.
  type: DurableObjectNamespace<SpaceObject>
  target: SpaceObject in this worker
  reads: SpaceEnv
```

```mdl
actor SpaceObject: The authority for one graph: it holds the records and hands out seqs.
  binding: SPACE
  key: the graph's slug — `idFromName(slug)`
  owns: the graph's records and their order
  storage: sqlite
  tables: [entries]
  keyspaces: [spaceState]
  alarm: Deletes all storage 24 hours after the first write; does not re-arm.
  ops:
    fetch(PushRequest) → PushResult
    webSocketMessage(ClientMessage) → RecordsMessage | PushResult
```

```mdl
table entries: The current version of one record of the graph.
  store: SpaceObject storage (no migration history; graphs are scratch)
  columns:
    key: TEXT PRIMARY KEY      # SyncRecord.key
    seq: INTEGER NOT NULL      # the stamp of the write that put this version here
    typename: TEXT NOT NULL
    props: TEXT NOT NULL       # json
    refs: TEXT NOT NULL        # json
    deleted: INTEGER NOT NULL  # 1 = tombstone
  key: key
  indexes:
    - entries_seq(seq): a pull reads everything above a seq, in order
```

```mdl
keyspace spaceState: The counters and dates of one graph.
  store: SpaceObject storage
  keys:
    seq: number                    # the highest seq handed out
    incarnation: string            # random, minted on first read after the store is empty
    createdAt: number              # epoch ms of the first write; the alarm fires 24h later
    client:<clientId>: number      # the highest clientSeq applied for that client
  bound: one `client:` key per client that ever pushed; dropped with the graph after 24 hours
```

```mdl
route sync: One push and its answer, for a peer that cannot hold a socket and for scripts.
  method: POST
  path: /api/space/:slug/sync
  auth: none
  input:
    body: PushRequest
  output: PushResult
```

```mdl
route socket: The live connection: pulls, pushes, and other clients' writes as they land.
  method: GET
  path: /api/space/:slug/socket
  auth: none
  output: WebSocket of ClientMessage in, RecordsMessage | PushResult out
```

## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: Ordering

  req F-1.1:
    when: the object applies a push
    then: it stamps each record, in the order sent, with the graph's next seq, in one transaction, and
          stores that seq as the graph's highest

  req F-1.2:
    when: any write is ordered
    then: the order is the seq alone; no wall-clock time takes part
```

```mdl
feat F-2: Compare-and-set

  req F-2.1:
    when: a push carries records with a `base`
    then: the object applies it only if every such record's `base` equals the seq it holds for that key
          (0 for a key it has never held); otherwise it applies none of the push

  req F-2.2:
    when: a push is refused
    then: the answer lists the refused keys in `conflicts` and carries every record above the push's
          `since`, so the client can merge and push again

  req F-2.3:
    when: a record carries no `base`
    then: it is written unconditionally
```

```mdl
feat F-3: Delivery

  req F-3.1:
    when: a push is applied
    then: the pusher gets a `PushResult`, and every other socket gets a `RecordsMessage` of the applied
          records with `from` set to the seq before them

  req F-3.2:
    when: a push arrives with a `client` and a `clientSeq` no higher than the last one applied for it
    then: it is answered as accepted and nothing is written again
```

```mdl
feat F-4: Size

  req F-4.1:
    when: a push would leave more than 1000 live records
    then: it is refused (413 on the route, an error message on the socket); a tombstone or an edit that
          does not grow the live set is never refused
```

```mdl
feat F-5: Expiry

  req F-5.1:
    when: 24 hours have passed since the first write
    then: the alarm deletes all storage, and the next store has a new `incarnation`
```

```mdl
feat F-6: Deployment

  req F-6.1:
    when: the "Deploy to Cloudflare" button is pressed on this directory's README
    then: the directory, copied alone and installed with npm, builds and deploys with the `SPACE`
          namespace provisioned from its wrangler config

  req F-6.2:
    when: the worker's entry module is loaded
    then: it exports only the fetch handler and `SpaceObject`, since the runtime reads every export as one
```

## Acceptance

```mdl
scenario T-1: Seqs are stamped in order
  given: an empty graph
  when: a push of two new records with base 0
  then: it is accepted with seqs 1 and 2, and the store's seq is 2
  verifies: [F-1.1]
```

```mdl
scenario T-2: A stale base refuses the whole push
  given: records a and b; another client moved a past the base this push names
  when: a push of a and b
  then: it is refused with conflicts [a], the answer carries a's current version, and b is unchanged
  verifies: [F-2.1, F-2.2]
```

```mdl
scenario T-3: A retried push is applied once
  given: a push from client c with clientSeq 1 was applied
  when: the same push arrives again
  then: it is answered as accepted and the store's seq does not move
  verifies: [F-3.2]
```

```mdl
scenario T-4: The pusher gets an ack and the others get records
  given: two sockets on one graph
  when: one pushes
  then: it receives an `ack`, and the other receives `records` with `from` 0
  verifies: [F-3.1]
```

```mdl
scenario T-5: The cap counts live records
  given: a graph at 1000 live records
  when: a push deletes one and creates one, then a push creates one
  then: the first is accepted and the second is refused
  verifies: [F-4.1]
```

```mdl
scenario T-6: An expired graph is a new incarnation
  given: a graph with writes
  when: its alarm runs and another client writes
  then: the store's incarnation differs from before
  verifies: [F-5.1]
```

## Changelog

```mdl
decision D-1: Sync orders writes with a sequence number the server keeps and a counter each client keeps, never with timestamps. A round is: the client pulls, merges, and pushes.
  date: 2026-11-10
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1, F-2, PushRequest]
  source: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LepGAYKGht2b6Gyq1s1W6W
```

```mdl
decision D-2: The sync server worker can be deployed with a "Deploy to Cloudflare" button.
  date: 2026-11-10
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-6]
  source: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LepGAYKGht2b6Gyq1s1W6W
```

```mdl
decision D-3: A push is compare-and-set per record and all or nothing; a refused push is answered with what the client missed. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-11-10
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-2, PushResult]
  why: |
    Applying writes in arrival order let a client overwrite a version it never saw. Refusing the whole
    push keeps a client's batch consistent with itself, and answering with the missed records saves the
    client a separate pull before it merges.
  rejected: |
    Per-record accept and reject, which applies half a batch; a version vector per record, which needs
    no central authority but this design has one in the Durable Object.
```

```mdl
decision D-4: `clientSeq` numbers a client's pushes so the object applies a retried push once. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-11-10
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-3.2, spaceState]
  why: A push whose answer was lost on a dropped socket is sent again; without the counter its now-stale bases would read as a conflict.
```

```mdl
decision D-5: The server is its own package whose directory imports nothing outside itself and pins its tools by version. Fills in [D-2].
  date: 2026-11-10
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-6]
  why: The button copies only the directory and installs it with npm, which resolves neither `workspace:` nor `catalog:` versions.
```
